# A vendored driver package is signed. Git must not touch a byte of it.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `input` on at least one machine here, which rewrites CRLF
# to LF on the way into a commit. That is exactly the edit the package cannot
# survive: `mttvdd.cat` holds a hash of the files beside it, so a line ending
# changed in transit voids the signature, and Windows then refuses the package
# or wants the machine in test-signing mode.
#
# It very nearly happened. `MttVDD.inf` came through untouched only because it
# is UTF-16 and git guessed binary from the NUL bytes; `vdd_settings.xml` is
# ASCII and was normalised on the first commit. Guessing is not a guarantee,
# and the next package to be vendored may have a plain-text file that is
# catalogued.
third_party/VirtualDisplayDriver/** -text

# The FFmpeg DLLs, built by scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh. Binary, so git neither
# diffs nor normalises them; PROVENANCE.md beside them holds their SHA-256,
# which a rewritten byte would no longer match.
third_party/ffmpeg/**/*.dll binary
